  ('205', '6', '3.4 Implementation', 'Batch normalization은 convolution 직후, activation 이전', '23', E'“We adopt batch normalization right after each convolution and before activation.”,
  Our implementation for ImageNet follows the practice in Krizhevsky2012; Simonyan2015. The image is resized with its shorter side randomly sampled in [256,480] for scale augmentation Simonyan2015. A 224 \\times 224 crop is randomly sampled from an image or its horizontal flip, with the per-pixel mean subtracted Krizhevsky2012. The standard color augmentation in Krizhevsky2012 is used.,
  We adopt batch normalization (BN) Ioffe2015 right after each convolution and before activation, following Ioffe2015.,
  We initialize the weights as in He2015 and train all plain/residual nets from scratch.,
  We use SGD with a mini-batch size of 256. The learning rate starts from 0.1 and is divided by 10 when the error plateaus, and the models are trained for up to 60\\times 10^{4} iterations. We use a weight decay of 0.0001 and a momentum of 0.9. We do not use dropout Hinton2012, following the practice in Ioffe2015.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:57:53.282277+00'),
  ('206', '6', '3.4 Implementation', 'ImageNet scale augmentation `[256,480]`', '24', E'“The image is resized with its shorter side randomly sampled in [256, 480].”,
  Our implementation for ImageNet follows the practice in Krizhevsky2012; Simonyan2015. The image is resized with its shorter side randomly sampled in [256,480] for scale augmentation Simonyan2015. A 224 \\times 224 crop is randomly sampled from an image or its horizontal flip, with the per-pixel mean subtracted Krizhevsky2012. The standard color augmentation in Krizhevsky2012 is used.,
  We adopt batch normalization (BN) Ioffe2015 right after each convolution and before activation, following Ioffe2015.,
  We initialize the weights as in He2015 and train all plain/residual nets from scratch.,
  We use SGD with a mini-batch size of 256. The learning rate starts from 0.1 and is divided by 10 when the error plateaus, and the models are trained for up to 60\\times 10^{4} iterations. We use a weight decay of 0.0001 and a momentum of 0.9. We do not use dropout Hinton2012, following the practice in Ioffe2015.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:57:53.282277+00'),
